  "hindi": "'शत्रु को आश्रय देने वाले या बने हुए काम को नष्ट करने वाले पार्ष्णिग्राह, आसार, मध्यम अथवा उदासीन राजा का प्रतिकार करना है; संकरे मार्ग को साफ करना है; कोश, दण्ड, मित्र, शत्रु या अटवी की सेना, अथवा विष्टि के लिए उपयुक्त ऋतु की प्रतीक्षा करनी है; शत्रु के बनाए हुए दुर्ग-कार्य, संचय और रक्षा-साधनों का क्षय, उसकी खरीदी हुई सेना की और मित्र-सेना की निराशा आ जाएगी; अथवा शत्रु-पक्ष में भेद डालने वाले हमारे लोग शीघ्रता नहीं करा रहे हैं; अथवा शत्रु स्वयं हमारे अभिप्राय को पूरा कर देगा' — ऐसा सोचकर वह धीरे-धीरे चले; इसके विपरीत स्थिति में शीघ्र चले।",
  "english": "(Thinking:) 'A heel-seizer, a reinforcer, a middle or a neutral king who would give shelter (to the enemy) or destroy what has been achieved has to be countered; a narrow road has to be cleared; the treasury, the army, the forces of the ally, the enemy or the forest tribes, or the season for labourers, have to be waited for; the exhaustion of the fort-works, stores and defences the enemy has made, the despondency of his hired troops and of his ally's troops will come about; or the instigators (planted in the enemy's camp) are not urging haste; or the enemy will himself fulfil (our) intended purpose' — he should march slowly; in the opposite case, quickly.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The clauses up to iti are the considerations for marching slowly. viṣṭi-ṛtu: the season when forced labour (viṣṭi) is available; alternatively 'the season of labour'. upajapitāraḥ: agents who sow dissension among the enemy; na-atitvarayanti could also be read 'are not in too great a hurry'. The e-text's '-' in ca-āgamiṣyati and na-atitvarayanti marks sandhi in the print.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
